The amount $X$ of bread in hundreds of kilos that a bakery sells in a day is a random variable with probability density function

$$
f(x)=\begin{cases}
cx, & 0\le x\le 3\\
c(6-x), & 3\le x\le 6\\
0, & \text{otherwise}
\end{cases}
$$

i. Find the value of $c$ which makes $f(x)$ a pdf.
ii. What is the probability that the amount of bread (in hundreds of kilos) that will be sold in a day is between 1.5 and 2.5.

Let $(X_1,X_2,\ldots,X_n)$ be a random sample of size $n$ from a distribution whose pmf is given by

$$
f(x;\theta)=\begin{cases}
\theta^x(1-\theta)^{1-x}, & x=0,1\text{ and }0\le \theta\le 1\\
0, & \text{otherwise}
\end{cases}
$$

Find the maximum likelihood estimator for $\theta$.
